.TH CHTTPSVR_ENGINE_STOP 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_engine_stop \- signal the engine to stop
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpserver.h>

void chttpsvr_engine_stop(void);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Signals the shared facil.io engine to stop accepting new connections and
begin draining in-flight requests.  Returns immediately; use
chttpsvr_engine_wait() to block until the drain completes.

Forces the engine down even if other references are still
outstanding (from other chttpsvr instances, or from chttpclient's
async engine, in the same process); the engine is shared, so this
also aborts any in-flight chttpclient async work
(chttpclient_do_async/_streaming, chttpclient_do_pooled/_streaming)
along with every chttpsvr listener.  This is an inherent consequence
of sharing one process-wide reactor for what is meant to be
process-shutdown-driven use, not a defect.

Non-blocking and async-signal-safe: it is safe to call this function
directly from a POSIX signal handler (e.g. SIGINT, SIGTERM).

The library does not install any signal handlers.  Applications are
responsible for wiring this function into whatever signal or shutdown
mechanism they use.

Safe to call before the engine has ever started (no-op).
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_engine_wait (3),
.BR chttpsvr_stop (3),
.BR chttpsvr_start (3)
